<DocsLayout title="Contributing" description="How to contribute safely to VulnWeave.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">CONTRIBUTING</p><h1>Help improve VulnWeave</h1><p class="lede">Contributions should preserve the project’s local-first, evidence-led model.</p>
    <h2>Before opening a change</h2><ol><li>Keep scanner integrations behind the Analyzer Adapter boundary.</li><li>Do not persist matched secret values in normalized findings or reports.</li><li>Make user-visible claims traceable to scanner or local static evidence.</li><li>Keep analysis advisory unless a user explicitly configures a reviewed gate.</li></ol>
    <h2>Validate your work</h2><pre><code>pnpm install&#10;pnpm check&#10;pnpm test&#10;pnpm docs:build</code></pre>
    <h2>Good first areas</h2><ul><li>Improve scanner normalization tests with safe, deterministic fixtures.</li><li>Improve documentation and plain-language guidance.</li><li>Add evidence-backed local graph relationships.</li><li>Improve accessibility or rendering of static reports and docs.</li></ul>
